// N112: token-serial FP32 gated delta-net (GDN) prompt recurrence for Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70) as a torch XPU op
// library (torch.ops.n112gdn.*). Drop-in for SGLang's chunk_gated_delta_rule extend call (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next linear
// attention layers): same inputs (q, k, v, g, beta, state pool + slot indices, cu_seqlens), same outputs (o, and the
// final recurrent state written back in place to the pool).
//
// Port of Strata's gdn_rec_cols_pipe_kernel (sycl/src/prefill/kernels.dp.cpp of github.com/Niko1221/Strata,
// HEAD 82f46a8): one work-group per (sequence, value head, block of value columns), each thread keeps a slice of its
// column's FP32 state in registers for the whole prompt, the next token's inputs are fetched while the current token
// computes. Adapted to SGLang:
//   * state pool [slots, H, V, K] (fp32, or bf16) indexed by the per-sequence slot (slot < 0: zero initial state and
//     no write-back, like the Triton kernel); value row v of head h is contiguous over k;
//   * varlen batches through cu_seqlens (device, no host sync), GQA head map hk = h / (H / Hk);
//   * q / k / v bf16 read in place from strided views of the conv output (no contiguous copies);
//   * q / k L2 normalisation (use_qk_l2norm_in_kernel) as per-(token, key head) inverse norms from a prepass, folded
//     into the recurrence: kv = rk * (S . k), S = e^g S + k (rk * beta * (v - e^g kv)), o = rq * scale * (S . q);
//   * the reductions over k run across the RG lanes that share a column (adjacent lanes of one sub-group) with
//     sub-group shuffles: no shared local memory and no work-group barrier in the token loop.
// Precision: fp32 state, products and accumulation; o rounded once to bf16 (RNE). The Triton chunk path rounds the
// normalised q / k, the WY factors and the per-chunk state to bf16, so this kernel is at least as close to an
// fp64 token-serial reference (test_gdn_xpu.py measures both).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
